=== focused evidence: T-013 (closing audit) — AC-028 and AC-029 ===

WHAT "FOCUSED" MEANS FOR THIS TASK, since it differs in kind from T-001..T-012.
T-013 adds NO suite: tasks.md:2713 puts "any new production script or schema"
out of scope, and the implementation report states "No new suite. This is a
closing audit task; its deliverable is measurement." There is therefore no
"T-013's own suite" to run. The focused evidence is instead the two acceptance
criteria the task owns — AC-028 (registration + the three-part protected-file
proof) and AC-029 (non-use declarations + CI-resilience checklist) — plus the
three suites T-013 actually edited.

Required Workflow is `acceptance-first` (tasks.md:2632), NOT `tdd`. There is
consequently no Red/Green log pair in this chain, and none is required: the
contract checker enforces red_evidence/green_evidence only when
required_workflow == "tdd" (check-contract.py:_pass5_tdd_evidence, early-returns
otherwise), and the risk->workflow rule that would force tdd applies only to
high/critical (check-contract.py:_pass5b_risk_workflow). T-013 is `medium`.

Every figure below was measured in THIS session against HEAD b3b2805e with a
clean working tree (`git status --porcelain` empty before and after).

