1. THE THREE SUITES T-013 EDITED — count-neutrality measured at BOTH ends
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

AC-029 required three `mktemp` fixture roots to be `pwd -P`-normalized. The fix
must not have removed an assertion. Rather than take the report's word, both the
BEFORE and AFTER states were run in this session.

AFTER (working tree at HEAD b3b2805e):

  $ bash tests/project-context-schema.tests.sh      exit=0   PASS: 44  FAIL: 0
  $ bash tests/approver-registry-schema.tests.sh    exit=0   PASS: 8   FAIL: 0
  $ bash tests/guard-staging-exemption.tests.sh     exit=0   33 passed, 0 failed

BEFORE (`git archive 71e0f0f2 | tar -x` into a scratch dir outside the repo;
71e0f0f2 is the commit immediately before T-013's first commit):

  $ bash tests/project-context-schema.tests.sh      exit=0   PASS: 44  FAIL: 0
  $ bash tests/approver-registry-schema.tests.sh    exit=0   PASS: 8   FAIL: 0
  $ bash tests/guard-staging-exemption.tests.sh     exit=0   33 passed, 0 failed

Identical in all three, so the edit is count-neutral by measurement and not only
by argument. The diff was also read in full (`git diff 71e0f0f2 HEAD -- <the
three>`): each file gains exactly +3 lines, two of them a comment citing
design.md Test Strategy item 12 and tests/lib/loop-driver.sh:124, and one of them
the normalization itself —

  WORK=$(cd "$WORK" && pwd -P)              (project-context-schema, approver-registry-schema)
  WORK="$(cd "$WORK" && pwd -P)"            (guard-staging-exemption)

— purely additive, with no deletion anywhere in the three hunks, so it is
structurally incapable of removing an assertion.

Note the third suite is `guard-staging-exemption`, which belongs to NO task's
Planned Files (it arrived with commit 67acc6cd). T-013 edited it anyway because
AC-029's scope is "every new suite", and it is registered in tests/run-all.sh.

