4. AC-028 PART 2b — the LIVE workflow is UNCHANGED, which is REQUIRED
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the part most easily misread as a defect, so it is stated plainly: the
live `.github/workflows/test.yml` being untouched is what AC-028 demands, not a
gap. The three-part shape is staged / live-unchanged / post-copy-registered.

  live sha256 (working tree, HEAD b3b2805e):
    3fe8466c4208dc89ea18811e71c5533b87fcc1977d49d83702697210482f86f4
  live sha256 (at merge-base b085ec76):
    3fe8466c4208dc89ea18811e71c5533b87fcc1977d49d83702697210482f86f4
  branch commits touching the live workflow:
    $ git log --oneline b085ec76..HEAD -- .github/workflows/test.yml  ->  0

  staged candidate sha256:
    c59b1c9a1367a32036fd072675fe7e8f75f8dc802f8703559bd799d04b7473ac
  MANIFEST.sha256 entry for that path:
    c59b1c9a1367a32036fd072675fe7e8f75f8dc802f8703559bd799d04b7473ac

The staged bytes and the manifest entry are the SAME digest; the live bytes are a
different digest. That is exactly the staged-not-yet-applied state.

Absence proved by a command that would have found the thing: a bare substring
grep — the loosest available — for each of the 13 suite names over the LIVE file
returns 0 for all 13. So the live workflow registers none of this epic's suites,
which is the pre-apply state the three-part proof requires.

CONSEQUENCE THAT LOOKS LIKE A FAILURE AND IS NOT. Run from the repository root,
where the manifest's paths resolve to the LIVE tree:

  $ shasum -a 256 -c specs/epic-189-a1-project-context/human-copy/MANIFEST.sha256
  .github/workflows/test.yml: FAILED
  specs/epic-189-a1-project-context/human-copy/PROTECTED-MANIFEST.md: OK
  plugins/sdd-quality-loop/references/guard-invariants.json: OK
  plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generate-guard-invariants.py: OK
  plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generated/guard_invariants.py: OK
  plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generated/guard-invariants.generated.js: OK
  plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generated/guard-invariants.generated.ps1: OK
  plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generated/guard-invariants.generated.sh: OK
  plugins/sdd-ship/skills/ship/SKILL.md: OK
  plugins/sdd-lite/skills/lite-spec/SKILL.md: OK
  shasum: WARNING: 1 computed checksum did NOT match
  exit=1

One FAILED, nine OK. The one FAILED is the workflow, and it reads FAILED
precisely BECAUSE the live file has not been published yet — the manifest pins
the staged bytes, and the live bytes are still the pre-apply ones. This is the
same shape ship/SKILL.md and lite-spec/SKILL.md presented before T-012's human
apply; both now read OK because that apply landed. Applying the workflow is a
final-phase action, outside T-013's Done When. NOT a failure and NOT a defect.

Measured the other way round — resolving every manifest path under human-copy/,
which is what the audit harness does — all TEN entries MATCH. Both readings are
correct and they are consistent: the staged tree matches the manifest completely,
the live tree matches it in nine of ten places, and the tenth is the pending
publication.

