6. AC-029 — non-use declarations and the CI-resilience checklist
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Re-derived directly over the 25 files, not read out of the committed artifact.

D1, real LLM / agent-CLI invocation at a COMMAND position. A `gh` invocation
would appear as `gh` followed by a subcommand at a command position; the scan
returns NO match across all 25 files. The harness's wider pattern
`(claude|codex|copilot|gh|sdd-sudo)` at a command position returns exactly two
lines in all 25 files, and both are the same assertion DESCRIPTION string, one
per lane:

  tests/check-hook-activation-handshake.tests.sh:172
    assert_exit "$rc" 0 "TEST-027 copilot-cli: a genuine --emit copilot deny JSON + matching nonce -> exit 0"
  tests/check-hook-activation-handshake.tests.ps1:165
    Assert-Eq $r.ExitCode 0 'TEST-027 copilot-cli: a genuine --emit copilot deny JSON + matching nonce -> exit 0'

Neither is a command; both are quoted text passed to an assertion helper.

D1b, ANY textual occurrence of `sdd-sudo|anthropic|openai|api.github.com|https?://`.
Four files are non-zero and each was opened and identified:

  tests/canonicalize-sdd-yaml.tests.sh   2  -> both are the YAML fixture value
  tests/canonicalize-sdd-yaml.tests.ps1  2     `http://example.com` (lines 441/442
                                               and 473/475), a round-trip fixture
  tests/hook-guard-epic-a1-boundary.tests.sh   1  -> the sentinel-file fixture CONTENT
  tests/hook-guard-epic-a1-boundary.tests.ps1  1     "enabled-by: human via /sdd-sudo"
                                                     (:140 and :130), a string literal
                                                     written into a mktemp fixture

An independent whole-word grep for `sdd-sudo` over all 25 files returns those two
lines and nothing else. So the epic contains ZERO `sdd-sudo` invocations and two
occurrences of the literal text inside fixture data. `anthropic`, `openai` and
`api.github.com` appear nowhere in any of the 25.

D1c, `SDD_SUDO`: present only in tests/generate-approval-sidecar.tests.sh as the
environment-variable NAMES `SDD_SUDO_KEY` / `SDD_SUDO_KEY_FILE` in the
key-resolution byte-parity fixtures, whose value is the literal
`"byte-parity-value"` (:392), popped at :398, re-set as a file at :400 and cleared
along with the other three key vars at :405. No live grant is taken.

D2, every `mktemp` root `pwd -P`-normalized: all 13 `.sh` suites report a
normalized root. Twelve are NORMALIZED_LATER (the assignment is on one line and
the normalization on the next), and check-hook-activation-handshake additionally
creates three nested roots (T027 L122, T032 L286, THARD L473) classified
NORMALIZED_INHERITED($WORK) because they are created under the already-normalized
$WORK. Zero NOT_NORMALIZED. The three that were violations before this task are
the three suites in section 1 above.

D3, possibly-empty bash array expanded under `set -u`: the hazard cannot arise,
because there is no array expansion at all. `grep -c '\[@\]'` returns 0 for every
one of the 13 `.sh` suites, individually:

  project-context-schema 0, canonicalize-sdd-yaml 0, generate-approval-sidecar 0,
  approver-registry-schema 0, detect-policy-weakening 0, validate-approval-sidecar 0,
  apply-human-copy 0, check-hook-activation-handshake 0, guard-invariants-epic-a1 0,
  hook-guard-epic-a1-boundary 0, plugin-contracts-track-selection 0,
  ship-track-selection-migration 0, guard-staging-exemption 0

POSITIVE CONTROL for that absence claim, because a grep that matches nothing
proves nothing on its own: the identical `grep -c '\[@\]'` against
tests/run-all.sh returns 1. The pattern does find array expansions when they are
there.

D4, `set -u` discipline: all 13 `.sh` suites set it — twelve as a bare `set -u`
and guard-staging-exemption as `set -euo pipefail` (:28).

